    "html": "<table><thead><tr><td>[RGB]25,55,105 white<b>Core Perspective</b></td><td>white<b>Key Research Contents</b></td><td>white<b>Representative Strategies & Works</b></td></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>[RGB]220,230,245 <b>Physical Property Estimation</b></td><td>Infer visual and mechanical properties that constrain object behavior; develop physically grounded representations and simulation-ready assets.</td><td>Neural Reflectance Fields ; Physion ; PhysBench ; QuantiPhy ; PhysX-3D ; PhysX-Anything</td></tr><tr><td><b>Affordance Reasoning</b></td><td>Infer feasible interaction regions and action modes conditioned on object geometry, physical properties, task context, and prior interaction experience.</td><td>AffordanceNet ; Where2Act ; RAIL ; RoboPoint ; PhysX-3D</td></tr><tr><td>[RGB]220,230,245 <b>Physical Consequence Prediction</b></td><td>Predict action-conditioned state transitions, temporal dynamics, and counterfactual outcomes for interaction planning and risk assessment.</td><td>CLEVRER ; CausalVQA ; world-model-based predictive frameworks</td></tr><tr><td><b>Physical Consistency Verification</b></td><td>Assess geometric, temporal, and physical validity of reconstructed, generated, or predicted scene states and simulation assets.</td><td>PhyGenBench ; video world-model analysis ; PhysX-Anything</td></tr><tr><td>[RGB]240,244,250 3>p18.6cm<b>Overall Goal</b>: Integrate geometry, physical properties, affordances, and action-conditioned dynamics into a physically grounded scene representation for reliable interaction and planning.</td></tr></tbody></table>"
